{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1187442-deity-wish-list-for-members-of-upcoming-pantheons","id":1187442,"title":"Deity Wish List for Members of Upcoming Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-18T20:19:56-08:00","id":1187442,"title":"Deity Wish List for Members of Upcoming Pantheons","content":"I realized that we have a thread requesting new pantheons and a thread requesting new members for existing pantheons, but not a thread requesting specific deities for pantheons that haven't been included yet. For this thread, I'd like to know which deities people would like to see the most for pantheons that aren't in the game yet, the less obvious, the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T00:27:12-08:00","id":1187481,"title":"","content":"Wait, so you're asking about the deities we want to see in other Pantheons, not additional ones for the 10 Pantheons in Hero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T06:26:47-08:00","id":1187534,"title":"","content":"Yes. For instance, which specific Bogovi, Atua, Anunna, etc. you'd like to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T17:04:16-08:00","id":1188023,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, but I'll say it again, the deity I'm most looking forward to is Asherah. There's just something fascinating about the way she was thrown down the memory hole in order to make room for patriarchal monotheism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1529-srgrvsalot","name":"SrGrvsaLot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:23:29-08:00","id":1188330,"title":"","content":"Which pantheons are supposed to be in the forthcoming books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:38:22-08:00","id":1188334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1187442-deity-wish-list-for-members-of-upcoming-pantheons?p=1188330#post1188330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which pantheons are supposed to be in the forthcoming books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Companion: Loa (afro-Caribbean), Nemetondevos (Gaulish), Yazata (Persian)<br /> <br /> Demigod: Eastern Slavic (Bogovi?), Anunna (Mesopotamian), Maya (K\u2019uh?), Atua (Polynesian), EITHER the Navajo/Apachean (Diyin Dine\u2019e?) or the Inca (Apu?)<br /> <br /> Arthurian supplement: Plant Don (Welsh)<br /> <br /> God: Elohim (Canaanite/Phoenician), probably whichever of the Diyin Dine\u2019e or Apu didn\u2019t make it into Demigod, the Palas (Vajrayana Buddhist), some form of Aboriginal Australian<br /> <br /> Mentioned as possible with no book indicated: Anga (Guarani)<br /> <br /> Others i\u2019d particularly hope for: Kachina (Hopi/Puebloan), Inue (Inuit), Jumalat (Finnish), Tngri (Mongol/Turkic), Milungu (Nyanga), Diwata (Tagalog), Shiunesh (Hittite, possibly a dead Pantheon like the Nemetondevos), fleshing out more gods and cosmology of the Orenda (Iroquis even as they share Virtues and Purview with the Manitou), same for the distinctly Roman \u201cNumina\u201d, possibly the Wakanpi (Plains Siouan)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-21-2018, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:52:25-08:00","id":1188355,"title":"","content":"Cool. Thanks. <br /> <br /> I'd love to see Ayizan, the Loa of the marketplace and commerce, because gods and goddesses of business are always fun. Her husband, Loco, the Loa of healers and plants, is also a potentially fun one. <br /> <br /> If the Numina get their own thing, Laverna, the goddess of thieves, cheats and the underworld would be potentially cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T17:40:39-08:00","id":1188720,"title":"","content":"I'd like expansion on gods who are part of another's writeup. Like expanded Mantle stuff for gods with several famous ones, or talk about Mictlantechutli a bit since his mechanics were slipped into his wife's writeup but not much about him directly.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that's actually what this thread is about, but I love the idea of expanded fluff for these kinds of things since as it is, they're given a bit but not as much as I'd like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T01:33:43-08:00","id":1188798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1187442-deity-wish-list-for-members-of-upcoming-pantheons?p=1188355#post1188355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Numina get their own thing, Laverna, the goddess of thieves, cheats and the underworld would be potentially cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, she's in my notes who would need to show up as something other than simply a Mantle for one of the Theoi. One of the only goddesses on that list actually. The big ones are Janus of course, and then the three deified &quot;fathers&quot; of Rome who I imagine ruling the Numina (in the name of Jupiter of course) as an imperial Triumvriate.<br /> <br /> Pater Indiges (Aeneas, Scion of Venus)<br /> Quirinus (Romulus, Scion of Mars - he inherited the Mantle from a Sabine War god he slew)<br /> Divis Julius (Julius Caesar, Scion of Venus)<br /> <br /> <br /> I can think of a lot of related lesser divinities under their authority (Rhea Silvia, Tiberinus, Juturna, Fontus, the various other deified emperors and deified relatives, etc) but obviously most of the big names are Theoi Mantles thanks to wear they cribbed their myths from and patched onto their separately existing religion (though in the World, lets defer to their own myths about themselves and assume the Latins were always Olympian worshipers by way of Aeneas).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T10:13:50-08:00","id":1188914,"title":"","content":"After Moana, I'd love to see Maui and Pele get a mention in Demigod.<br /> <br /> That I have a concept character who's a daughter of Pele is completely unrelated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T16:10:36-08:00","id":1189033,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that a Wild West book would be a cool place to include several Native pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T05:50:14-08:00","id":1189204,"title":"","content":"For the Greeks I'd like Iris, Demeter, Hestia, Hecate, and Heracles, included. <br /> <br /> For the Egyptians l'd like Hathor and Nephtis (forgive my spelling)<br /> <br /> For the Tuatha l'd like some changes like the death purview for Brigid. The only thing Brigid does in the mythological cycle is invent keening, a formal mourning for the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T08:18:06-08:00","id":1189232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_pos